Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant tables / columns and how they will be used

bigquery‑public‑data.census_bureau_usa.population_by_zip_2010  
• zipcode : to join with zipcode_area and to aggregate population  
• population : numeric value to be summed  
• gender : we will keep only ‘male’ and ‘female’ records (ignoring rows where gender is NULL/empty = overall total)  
• minimum_age / maximum_age : both must be NULL so that the record represents the “all‑ages” total for that gender  

bigquery‑public‑data.utility_us.zipcode_area  
• zipcode : join key to population table  
• zipcode_geom : polygon of the ZCTA; will be cast to GEOGRAPHY with ST_GEOGFROMTEXT()  
• area_land_meters / area_water_meters : required in result  
• latitude / longitude : centroid of the zip area – to be returned  
• state_code / state_name / city / county : descriptive columns to be returned  

Conditions that will be used  
1. population_by_zip_2010.gender IN ('male','female')  
2. population_by_zip_2010.minimum_age IS NULL AND population_by_zip_2010.maximum_age IS NULL  
3. ST_DWITHIN( ST_GEOGFROMTEXT(zipcode_geom), ST_GEOGPOINT(-122.3321, 47.6062), 10000 )

--------------------------------------------------------------------
Ten exploratory → final queries
--------------------------------------------------------------------

```sql
--Description: 1) Quick look at the 2010 population table.
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_usa.population_by_zip_2010`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) How many rows have NULL ages and a non‑empty gender?
SELECT gender, COUNT(*) AS rows_with_all_ages
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_usa.population_by_zip_2010`
WHERE minimum_age IS NULL
  AND maximum_age IS NULL
  AND gender IN ('male','female')
GROUP BY gender;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Distinct values found in the gender column.
SELECT DISTINCT gender
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_usa.population_by_zip_2010`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Sample of male & female “all‑ages” rows.
SELECT zipcode, gender, population
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_usa.population_by_zip_2010`
WHERE minimum_age IS NULL
  AND maximum_age IS NULL
  AND gender IN ('male','female')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Aggregate the male+female all‑age population per ZIP code for the whole U.S.
SELECT zipcode,
       SUM(population) AS total_pop_mf_2010
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_usa.population_by_zip_2010`
WHERE minimum_age IS NULL
  AND maximum_age IS NULL
  AND gender IN ('male','female')
GROUP BY zipcode
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Which ZIP polygons are within 10 km of the point (‑122.3321, 47.6062)?
SELECT zipcode
FROM `bigquery-public-data.utility_us.zipcode_area`
WHERE ST_DWITHIN(
        ST_GEOGFROMTEXT(zipcode_geom),
        ST_GEOGPOINT(-122.3321, 47.6062),
        10000)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Show land/water area and centroid for ZIPs near the point.
SELECT zipcode,
       area_land_meters,
       area_water_meters,
       latitude,
       longitude
FROM `bigquery-public-data.utility_us.zipcode_area`
WHERE ST_DWITHIN(
        ST_GEOGFROMTEXT(zipcode_geom),
        ST_GEOGPOINT(-122.3321, 47.6062),
        10000)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Join step – attach summed population to ZIP areas within 10 km.
SELECT z.zipcode,
       p.total_pop_mf_2010,
       z.area_land_meters,
       z.area_water_meters
FROM (
    SELECT zipcode,
           SUM(population) AS total_pop_mf_2010
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_usa.population_by_zip_2010`
    WHERE minimum_age IS NULL
      AND maximum_age IS NULL
      AND gender IN ('male','female')
    GROUP BY zipcode
) AS p
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.utility_us.zipcode_area` AS z
ON p.zipcode = z.zipcode
WHERE ST_DWITHIN(
        ST_GEOGFROMTEXT(z.zipcode_geom),
        ST_GEOGPOINT(-122.3321, 47.6062),
        10000)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Add descriptive columns (state, city, county) and polygon itself.
SELECT z.zipcode,
       z.zipcode_geom,
       z.state_code,
       z.state_name,
       z.city,
       z.county,
       z.area_land_meters,
       z.area_water_meters,
       z.latitude,
       z.longitude,
       p.total_pop_mf_2010
FROM (
    SELECT zipcode,
           SUM(population) AS total_pop_mf_2010
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_usa.population_by_zip_2010`
    WHERE minimum_age IS NULL
      AND maximum_age IS NULL
      AND gender IN ('male','female')
    GROUP BY zipcode
) AS p
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.utility_us.zipcode_area` AS z
ON p.zipcode = z.zipcode
WHERE ST_DWITHIN(
        ST_GEOGFROMTEXT(z.zipcode_geom),
        ST_GEOGPOINT(-122.3321, 47.6062),
        10000)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) FINAL – return the requested columns for every ZCTA whose polygon
--               centroid lies within 10 km of (‑122.3321, 47.6062).
SELECT
  z.zipcode,
  z.zipcode_geom AS polygon,
  z.area_land_meters,
  z.area_water_meters,
  z.latitude,
  z.longitude,
  z.state_code,
  z.state_name,
  z.city,
  z.county,
  p.total_pop_mf_2010 AS total_population
FROM `bigquery-public-data.utility_us.zipcode_area` AS z
JOIN (
    SELECT
      zipcode,
      SUM(population) AS total_pop_mf_2010
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_usa.population_by_zip_2010`
    WHERE minimum_age IS NULL
      AND maximum_age IS NULL
      AND gender IN ('male','female')
    GROUP BY zipcode
) AS p
ON z.zipcode = p.zipcode
WHERE ST_DWITHIN(
        ST_GEOGFROMTEXT(z.zipcode_geom),
        ST_GEOGPOINT(-122.3321, 47.6062),
        10000)
ORDER BY total_population DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

